description:
Real bug found live-debugging e70.39: the shared cache signal (AppGroupCache.isMostRecentFetchAttemptFailing, added in e70.39) WAS being written correctly -- confirmed directly on disk at ~/Library/Group Containers/group.solutions.bluegull.aqi/Library/Preferences/, with aqi-last-failed-fetch-at genuinely more recent than aqi-last-successful-fetch-at. But AQIRefreshController.refreshNow() only calls WidgetCenter.shared.reloadTimelines(ofKind:) on the SUCCESS branch, never on the AQIFetchError catch branch. So even though the signal was correct, nothing ever told a placed widget to go re-check it -- it just sat on its old timeline until its own WidgetKit-scheduled reload eventually fired (up to an hour away), which is what Steve was actually observing when he said widgets still showed fresh data even after removing and re-adding.

Also surfaced along the way: {
    "aqi-last-successful-fetch-at" = {length = 16, bytes = 0x3830373536313438302e373134363331};
    "menu-bar-location-selection-mirror" = {length = 9, bytes = 0x2263757272656e7422};
    "refresh-schedule-install-offset" = {length = 18, bytes = 0x323732352e36383733303037393337363834};
} from a plain unsandboxed shell does NOT read the same file the sandboxed app actually uses -- the real App Group container lives at ~/Library/Group Containers/group.solutions.bluegull.aqi/Library/Preferences/group.solutions.bluegull.aqi.plist. Worth remembering for future live debugging of this app's shared state.
